Enhancement: Select bounded RAM, KV, or automatic working state for backup, import and check

Vaultic now accepts --working-memory-mode=ram|kv|auto on backup, check,
index import and index check, with shared RAM, scratch and disk budgets and
equivalent profile/environment settings. Automatic mode uses verified,
one-way fallback for disposable working state. Strict RAM never spills
working state; unsafe limits and exhaustion return actionable errors.

The budget covers managed working state, not whole-process RSS. Configure
co-resident reserves for other workloads. Omitting these controls preserves
existing behavior; metadata authority and publication semantics are unchanged.